# tally 2.2.1 (S-window-key, option A), L §4.6 Reading at a date: an item keyed by one time index, read with a date,
# "reads the key whose period holds it"; L §4.4: an operation "one value when the two agree", a key needing one value.
# conv and convm are dated w = window(2026-03-10, 2026-03-12): fxm, keyed by months, holds the whole window in
# 2026-03, so flows(convm, 2026-03) is 400.00 PLN; fx, keyed by days, is the hole (f2), and so is the balance that
# books both (f1). tally 2.2 gave the hole for both (the critic's fx.tally).
# tally 2.3 (G1, #247): restated so the moves are dated by a plain day and only their amounts read the
# window as a key: a window that reaches a move's `on` is a hole day (L §4.4).
=== fx.tally
model c_fx
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input w: date

input pday: date

input eur: num

input fx[d in days]: num PLN

input fxm[m in months]: num PLN

move conv: transfers
  on pday
  leg cash from world to konto amount round(eur * fx[w], minor(PLN), half-up)

move convm: transfers
  on pday
  leg cash from world to konto amount round(eur * fxm[w], minor(PLN), half-up)

version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  eur = 100 "c"
  pday = 2026-03-12 "c"
  w = window(2026-03-10, 2026-03-12) "c"
  fx[2026-03-01..2026-03-31] = 4 PLN "c"
  fxm[2026-03] = 4 PLN "c"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"

ask f1: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask f2: flows(conv, 2026-03), flows(convm, 2026-03)
ask f3: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) with w = 2026-03-11
=== expect
f1: ?"date within window(2026-03-10, 2026-03-12) not precise enough for a key" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
f2: (?"date within window(2026-03-10, 2026-03-12) not precise enough for a key" (w), 400.00 PLN)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
f3: 800.00 PLN
  pinned: w = 2026-03-11
  cut 2026-01-01
